          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em standard Courant Lie algebroid
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a type of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Courant+algebroid"} Courant algebroid
            constructed from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cotangent+bundle"} cotangent bundle
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+complex+geometry"} generalized complex geometry
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Recall from the discussion at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Courant+algebroid"} Courant algebroid
            that there are the following two equivalent definitions of Courant algebroids:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                as a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
                equipped with a bracket and a bilinear form on its space of sections, satisfying various identities;
            %li
              %p
                as a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-infinity+algebroid"} Lie 2-algebroid
                equivalently encoded in its
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley%E2%80%93Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley–Eilenberg algebra
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-manifolds"} dg-manifolds
          %h3#as_a_vector_bundle_with_extra_structure As a vector bundle with extra structure
          %p
            In the first perspective a
            %em standard Courant algebroid
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is the vector bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo =
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊕
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mo *
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E = T X\oplus T^* X
            – the fiberwise
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
            and the cotangent bundle – with
          %ul
            %li
              %p bilinear form
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mi X
                      %mo +
                      %mi ξ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo +
                      %mi η
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %mo =
                      %mi η
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo +
                      %mi ξ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\langle X + \xi , Y +\eta \rangle = \eta(X) + \xi(Y)
              %p
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y \in \Gamma(T X)
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ξ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi η
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi T
                        %mo *
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi, \eta \in \Gamma(T^* X)
            %li
              %p brackets
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi X
                      %mo +
                      %mi ξ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo +
                      %mi η
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo +
                      %msub
                        %mi ℒ
                        %mi X
                      %mi η
                      %mo −
                      %msub
                        %mi ℒ
                        %mi Y
                      %mi ξ
                      %mo +
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mn 2
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi η
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo −
                      %mi ξ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      [X + \xi, Y + \eta] = [X,Y] + \mathcal{L}_X \eta
                      \- \mathcal{L}_Y \xi + \frac{1}{2} d (\eta(X) - \xi(Y))
              %p
                where
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℒ
                        %mi X
                      %mi η
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi d
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi ι
                        %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mi η
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}_X \eta = \{d,\iota_X\} \eta
                denotes the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+derivative"} Lie derivative
                of the 1-form
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi η
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
                by the vector field
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %h3#as_a_dgmanifold As a dg-manifold
          %p
            As an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-manifold"} dg-manifold
            a standard Courant algeebroid is is
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                    %msup
                      %mi T
                      %mo *
                    %mi Π
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi T^* \Pi T X
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shifted+tangent+bundle"} shifted tangent bundle
          %p
            where the differential (homological vector field) is on each local coordinate patch
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi U
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n \simeq U \subset X
            with coordinates
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{x^i\}
                in degree 0
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi d
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{d x^i\}
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi θ
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\theta_i\}
                in degree 1
            %li
              %p
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{p_i\}
                in degree 2
          %p given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi d
                            %mi C
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi d
                            %mi dR
                          %mo +
                          %msub
                            %mi p
                            %mi i
                          %mfrac
                            %mo ∂
                            %mrow
                              %mo ∂
                              %msub
                                %mi θ
                                %mi i
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mi d
                          %msup
                            %mi x
                            %mi i
                          %mfrac
                            %mo ∂
                            %mrow
                              %mo ∂
                              %msup
                                %mi x
                                %mi i
                          %mo +
                          %msub
                            %mi p
                            %mi i
                          %mfrac
                            %mo ∂
                            %mrow
                              %mo ∂
                              %msub
                                %mi θ
                                %mi i
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  d_C &amp;= d_{dR} + p_i \frac{\partial}{\partial \theta_i}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;= d x^i \frac{\partial}{\partial x^i }
                  + p_i \frac{\partial}{\partial \theta_i}
                  \\end{aligned}
                  \\,.
          %h3#as_a_lie_2algebroid As a Lie 2-algebroid
          %p
            We may read the above
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
            as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley%E2%80%93Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley–Eilenberg algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔠
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE(\mathfrak{c}(X))
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+%E2%88%9E-algebroid"} Lie 2-algebroid
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔠
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{c}(X)
          %p More on this in the discussion below.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#as_the_atiyah_lie_2algebroid_of_a_gerbe
            As the Atiyah Lie 2-algebroid of a
            = succeed "-gerbe" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
          %p
            A standard Courant algebroid may be understood as being related to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}U(1)
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+2-bundle"} principal 2-bundle
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
            = succeed "s)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gerbe"} gerbe
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah+Lie+algebroid"} Atiyah Lie algebroid
            is related to a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+U%281%29-bundle"} principal U(1)-bundle
          %p (…explain…)
          %h3#connections_and_generalized_riemannian_metrics Connections and generalized Riemannian metrics
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔠
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{c}(X)
            for the standard Courant algebroid of the manifold
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+Lie+algebroid"} tangent Lie algebroid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T X
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi π
                  %mo :
                  %mi 𝔠
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\pi : \mathfrak{c}(X) \to X
                  \\,.
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mo :
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝔠
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\sigma : T X \to \mathfrak{c}(X)
          %p
            of this morphism of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+%E2%88%9E-algebroid"} Lie ∞-algebroid
            %em connection
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔠
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{c}(X)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebroid+valued+differential+forms"} ∞-Lie algebroid valued differential form
            data on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              On base manifolds of the form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = \mathbb{R}^n
              sections of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔠
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{c}(X) \to T X
              in the 1-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+%E2%88%9E-algebroid"} Lie ∞-algebroid
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mi X
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mi T
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q \in \Gamma(T X \oplus T X)
          %p
            The proof is straightforward and easy, but spelling it out in detail also serves to establish concepts and notation for the treatment of the Courant algebroid in terms of its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley%E2%80%93Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley–Eilenberg algebra
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley%E2%80%93Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley–Eilenberg algebra
              of the Lie 2-algebroid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔠
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{c}(\mathbb{R}^n)
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semifree+dga"} semifree dga
              whose underlying algebra is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grassmann+algebra"} Grassmann algebra
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔠
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msubsup
                        %mo ∧
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mn ∞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %msup
                        %mi ξ
                        %mi i
                      %msubsup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo =
                          %mn 1
                        %mi n
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %msub
                        %mi θ
                        %mi i
                      %msubsup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo =
                          %mn 1
                        %mi n
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mi i
                      %msubsup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo =
                          %mn 1
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝔠
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    CE(\mathfrak{c}(X))
                    \=
                    \\left(
                    \\wedge_{C^\infty(X)}^\bullet
                    ( \langle \xi^i \rangle_{i=1}^n
                    \\oplus
                    \\langle \theta_i \rangle_{i=1}^n
                    \\oplus
                    \\langle p_i \rangle_{i=1}^n
                    )
                    \\,,
                    d_{\mathfrak{c}(X)}
                    \\right)
            %p
              where the generators
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ξ
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi_i
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta_i
              are in degree 1 and the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_i
              in degree 2, equipped with the differential
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔠
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_{\mathfrak{c}(X)}
              that is defined on generators by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔠
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi ξ
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d_{\mathfrak{c}(X)} : x^i =  \xi^i
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔠
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi ξ
                      %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d_{\mathfrak{c}(X)} : \xi^i = 0
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔠
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d_{\mathfrak{c}(X)} : \theta_i = p_i
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔠
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d_{\mathfrak{c}(X)} : p_i = 0
                    \\,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{x^i\}_{i=1}^n
              are the canonical coordinate functions on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley%E2%80%93Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley–Eilenberg algebra
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+Lie+algebroid"} tangent Lie algebroid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T X
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deRham+complex"} deRham complex
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi dR
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    CE(T X ) = (\Omega^\bullet(X), d_{dR})
                    \\,.
            %p
              The morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔠
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{c}(X) \to T X
              is given by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
              morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi dR
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔠
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\Omega^\bullet(X),d_{dR}) \hookrightarrow
                    CE(\mathfrak{c}(X))
            %p
              that is the identity on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X)
              and identifies the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ξ
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi^i
              with the deRham differentials of the standard coordinate functions
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                    %mo ↦
                    %msup
                      %mi ξ
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d x^i \mapsto \xi^i
                    \\,.
            %p
              A section
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝔠
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma : \mathfrak{c}(X) \to T X
              is accordingly a dg-algebra morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi σ
                      %mo *
                    %mo :
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔠
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi dR
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\sigma^* : CE(\mathfrak{c}(X)) \to (\Omega^\bullet(X), d_{dR})
                    \\,.
            %p
              Being a section, it has to be the identity on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X)
              and send
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ξ
                        %mi i
                      %mo ↦
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mi dR
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi^i \mapsto d_{dR} x^i
            %p
              The image of the generators
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi θ
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta_i
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X)
              of the degree-1 elements in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\bullet(X)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              in question by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mi i
                    %mo ↦
                    %msub
                      %mi q
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} d
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\hat{t}_i \mapsto q_{i j} \d x^i
                    \\,.
            %p
              For this assignment to qualify as part of a morphism of dg-algebras, it has in addition to be compatible with the differential. The condition is that for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              we have the equality in the bottom right corner of
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi θ
                              %mi i
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ↦
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi d
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi 𝔠
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mi X
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi p
                              %mi i
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi σ
                                    %mo *
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi σ
                                    %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi q
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mi j
                            %mi d
                            %msup
                              %mi x
                              %mi j
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ↦
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi d
                                  %mi dR
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mo ∂
                              %mi k
                            %msub
                              %mi q
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mi j
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi d
                            %msup
                              %mi x
                              %mi k
                            %mo ∧
                            %mi d
                            %msup
                              %mi x
                              %mi j
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi s
                              %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi p
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\theta_i &amp;\stackrel{d_{\mathfrak{c}(X)}}{\mapsto}&amp;&amp; p_i
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\sigma^*}}
                    \&amp;&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\sigma^*}}
                    \\\
                    q_{i j} d x^j &amp;\stackrel{d_{dR}}{\mapsto}&amp;
                    (\partial_k q_{i j}) d x^k \wedge d x^j
                    \= &amp;
                    s^*(p_i)
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              This uniquely fixes the image under
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi σ
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma^*
              of the generators
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_i
              and the differential is respected. So, indeed, the section
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi σ
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma^*
              is specified by the tensor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q \in \Gamma(T X \otimes T X)
              and every such tensor gives rise to a section.
          %p
            The rank-2 tensor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            appearing in the above may be uniquely writtes as sum of a symmetric and a skew-symmetric rank-2 tensor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Sym
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \Gamma(Sym^2(T X))
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mn 2
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in \Gamma(\wedge^2 T X)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                  %mo =
                  %mi g
                  %mo +
                  %mi b
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  q = g + b
                  \\,.
          %p
            If the symmetric part happens to be non-degenerate, it may be regarded as a (possibly
            = succeed "-)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-Riemannian+metric"} pseudo
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} Riemannian metric
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                  %mo =
                  %mi g
                  %mo +
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q = g + b
            is called a
            %strong generalized Riemannian metric
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+complex+geometry"} generalized complex geometry
          %h3#canonical_lie_algebroid_3cocycle
            Canonical
            = succeed "-Lie" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            The standard Courant albebroid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔠
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{c}(X)
            is canonically equipped with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+%E2%88%9E-algebroid+cohomology"} Lie ∞-algebroid 3-cocycle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔠
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu \in CE(\mathfrak{c}(X))
            that is on a local patch
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi U
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n \simeq U \to X
            given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi U
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi ξ
                    %mi i
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mi i
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mu|_U = \xi^i \wedge p_i
                  \\,.
          %h3#morphisms_between_standard_courant_algebroids Morphisms between standard Courant algebroids
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              In the 1-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              of
              = succeed "s," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+%E2%88%9E-algebroid"} Lie ∞-algebroid
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism"} automorphism
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔠
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{c}(\mathbb{R}^n)
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  respect the projection
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔠
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi T
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{c}(X) \to T X
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi 𝔠
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi X
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo →
                                  %mi f
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mi 𝔠
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi X
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo ↘
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo ↙
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mi T
                                %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        \\mathfrak{c}(X) &amp;&amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp;&amp; \mathfrak{c}(X)
                        \\\
                        \&amp; \searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow
                        \\\
                        \&amp;&amp; T X
                        }
              %li
                %p
                  fix the canonical 3-cocycle
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi μ
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mi ξ
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu = \xi^i p_i
            %p
              come from (…say this more precisely…) rank-2 tensors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                    %mo =
                    %mi g
                    %mo +
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q = g + b
              such that the skew symmetric part
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
              is a closed 2-form,
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mi dR
                      %mi b
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_{dR} b = 0
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              With the same kind of reasoning as above, we find that the action on the generators
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta_i
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_i
              is of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi θ
                              %mi i
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ↦
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi d
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi 𝔠
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mi X
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi p
                              %mi i
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo *
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi θ
                              %mi i
                            %mo +
                            %msub
                              %mi q
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mi j
                            %msup
                              %mi θ
                              %mi i
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ↦
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi d
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi 𝔠
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mi X
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi p
                              %mi i
                            %mo +
                            %msub
                              %mo ∂
                              %mi k
                            %msub
                              %mi q
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mi j
                            %msup
                              %mi θ
                              %mi k
                            %mo ∧
                            %msup
                              %mi θ
                              %mi j
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi f
                              %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi p
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\theta_i &amp;\stackrel{d_{\mathfrak{c}(X)}}{\mapsto}&amp;&amp; p_i
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{f^*}}
                    \&amp;&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f^*}}
                    \\\
                    \\theta_i + q_{i j} \theta^i  &amp;
                    \\stackrel{d_{\mathfrak{c}(X)}}{\mapsto}&amp;
                    p_i
                    +
                    \\partial_k q_{i j} \theta^k \wedge \theta^j
                    \= &amp;
                    f^*(p_i)
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              For the 3-cocycle to be preserved,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ξ
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi ξ
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*(\xi^i p_i) = \xi^i p_i
              we need that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mi q
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                    %msup
                      %mi θ
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∧
                    %msup
                      %mi θ
                      %mi k
                    %mo ∧
                    %msup
                      %mi θ
                      %mi j
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                    %msup
                      %mi θ
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∧
                    %msup
                      %mi θ
                      %mi k
                    %mo ∧
                    %msup
                      %mi θ
                      %mi j
                    %mo =
                    %msup
